From: tompta1 <546706+tompta1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:39:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8011-pro2: Add storage, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth,
 touch and sound

Describe the iPad Pro 2's wiring in the dtsi its four boards share. Their
iPadOS 17.7.11 (21H461) device trees differ only in the panel, the touch
personality, the Wi-Fi module instance and, on the cellular boards, the
baseband, so every board gets it:

- storage on PCIe port 0 (NVMe through the NVMMU, host memory buffer from
  the boot loader) and the BCM4355 Wi-Fi on port 2, powered by the D2401's
  GPIO 1 and the WLAN UART;
- Bluetooth on UART3, linked to the Wi-Fi node for its module vendor;
- the K1 touch controller on SPI3 with its supply, LDO, sync pins and
  clock;
- headphones (CS42L83 on MCA4 through the AOP pads) and the two PDM
  microphones;
- the AOP with its motion sensors and microphone clock, and the video
  decoder;
- the BQ27540 battery gauge on UART5 (HDQ);
- the Smart Cover hall sensor on D2400 GPIO 0, with both hall events as
  wake events;
- the August touch analog supply and backlight.

The boards name their touch firmware, panel size, Bluetooth and Wi-Fi
board type and sound cards.

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf),
 kernel/patches/devices/t8011/0001-0020 reworked: moved from
 t8011-j120.dts into t8011-pro2.dtsi for all four boards; the trial
 charging variants (t8011-j120-charging*.dts), the D2355 charger, the
 Orion VBUS ADC, the speakers, the CT709 light sensors and the display
 controller left out with their drivers; the cover through the D2400 GPIO
 and gpio-keys instead of a cover driver; the Wi-Fi node powered by the
 existing BCM4355 sequence with the ADT's device-wake GPIO 164; the
 Bluetooth vendor through "apple,wlan"; identity mount matrices and the
 AOP target (filled in by the boot loader) dropped.]

Assisted-by: LLM
